data.body:
Another instance of circular dependency where GoapEvaluator delegates back to GraphManager. This pattern should be avoided as it defeats the purpose of extracting GOAP logic. The graph operations should be implemented directly in GoapEvaluator or extracted to a shared utility.
```suggestion
            # Example implementation of graph-related logic
            graph = world_state.graph
            neighbors = list(graph.neighbors(node))
            action_costs = {neighbor: graph[node][neighbor].get('cost', inf) for neighbor in neighbors}
            viability = {neighbor: graph[node][neighbor].get('viability', False) for neighbor in neighbors}
            result = {
                "action_costs": action_costs,
                "viability": viability,
                "goal_fulfillment": goal in neighbors
            }
```
